ype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX066\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"States that the board may designate 'the fund's investment adviser', which covers the adviser. It never says a sub-adviser can't be the designee. Under the '40 Act both are 'investment advisers', so the exclusion isn't implied.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers the at-least-quarterly written assessments to the board. It omits the designee's annual assessment of the valuation process.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Says the designee must 'report promptly on significant valuation matters', which covers material-matter reporting. It omits the board-set deadline and the 5-business-day maximum.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"There is no central error. The answer never says a sub-adviser can be the designee, and it affirms periodic written reporting. Coverage sums to 1.5 of 3 required points, which meets the half threshold, and core facts are supplied. The answer isn't correct because the sub-adviser exclusion, the annual assessment and the 5-business-day deadline are all missing. Some side claims fall outside the supplied evidence: 'officer or employee of the adviser' as designee and recordkeeping under Rule 31a-1. The evidence doesn't contradict them, so they aren't treated as material falsehoods.\"}","ttft_ms":6077,"type":"result","duration_ms":9630,"uuid":"80187343-7ad1-48ec-9f58-68af44600b53","ttft_stream_ms":552,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":553,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
